  "summary": "Malicious code in devplatform-react-query-clients (npm)",
  "details": "On require(), the package loads a bundled adapter that downloads a platform-specific binary payload over HTTPS from Cloudflare Workers hosts (oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev) at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, or /pkg/package.exe depending on OS/arch. If those hosts are unreachable it retrieves the payload in base64 chunks via DNS TXT records from the wel1[.]ru domain family (c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, ext[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, pkg[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru). The downloaded binary is written to /tmp/.cache_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt; (or %TEMP%\\dotnet_diag_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt;.exe on Windows), made executable, and launched as a detached background process. The package otherwise ships no functional SDK code.",
